/// Term 5: "Light and Dark" (Weeks 17-20) continues Year 1 Science's
/// pathway with a physics-adjacent strand, deliberately guarding against
/// the most common Year 1 light misconceptions -- Week 17 introduces
/// light sources (sun, torch, candle) versus things that only reflect
/// light (a mirror, and the moon, which is never described as making
/// its own light); Week 18 covers day and night at a simple,
/// age-appropriate level (the sun's light reaching where we are, not a
/// technical Earth-rotation explanation, and never framed as the sun
/// "turning off"); Week 19 covers shadows -- formed when something
/// solid blocks light, appearing on the side away from the light
/// source, with transparent objects making little or no shadow; Week 20
/// closes the term with a capstone combining light sources, day/night,
/// and shadows in one story, the same way Terms 1-4's own capstones
/// worked.
