/// Term 6: "Sound" (Weeks 21-24) continues Year 1 Science's pathway with
/// a second physics-adjacent strand -- Week 21 introduces sound as
/// caused by vibration (a drum skin, a plucked string, vocal cords, a
/// bell); Week 22 teaches that loud/quiet (volume) and high/low (pitch)
/// are two DIFFERENT properties of sound, deliberately not conflated;
/// Week 23 covers identifying everyday environmental sounds and their
/// sources, plus the simple idea that sound can be muffled/blocked;
/// Week 24 closes the term with a capstone combining vibration, volume/
/// pitch, and everyday sounds in one story, the same way Terms 1-5's
/// own capstones worked.
