/// Term 7 ("Decimals") of the Year 4 Mathematics pathway -- a natural
/// extension of Term 5's fractions work. Week 25 introduces tenths as
/// decimals (a fraction with denominator 10, e.g. 3/10 = 0.3), reading/
/// writing one-decimal-place numbers, and placing them on a number line
/// between whole numbers; Week 26 introduces hundredths as decimals
/// (denominator 100, e.g. 45/100 = 0.45) and connects tenths and
/// hundredths (0.3 = 0.30 = 30/100, while 0.03 is a different, smaller
/// value); Week 27 covers comparing/ordering decimals by place-value
/// column (tenths first, then hundredths -- never as whole numbers, so
/// 0.5 > 0.45 despite "45" looking bigger than "5") and rounding a
/// decimal to the nearest whole number; Week 28 closes the term with a
/// capstone -- a single "Nova School Athletics Records" scenario
/// (sprint times and jump distances to 1-2 decimal places) requiring
/// reading/writing, comparing/ordering, AND rounding decimals together,
/// reusing every skill from Weeks 25-27. Content was authored by four
/// parallel worktree-isolated agents (one per week) and independently
/// re-verified end to end (every decimal fact, place-value comparison,
/// and rounding case) before being spliced in here.
