/// Year 5 Mathematics full-year pathway. Follows Zin Min, a Nova School
/// student, across a full academic year of maths topics: Term 1 (Weeks
/// 1-4) number and place value up to 1,000,000, negative numbers,
/// rounding, and Roman numerals; Term 2 (Weeks 5-8) mental and formal
/// written addition and subtraction, closing with a multi-step
/// fundraiser problem-solving studio; Term 3 (Weeks 9-12) multiples,
/// factors, primes, and multiplication; Term 4 (Weeks 13-16) short
/// division and fractions, closing with a bake-sale division studio;
/// Term 5 (Weeks 17-20) multiplying fractions, decimals, and
/// percentages; Term 6 (Weeks 21-24) units of measurement, perimeter,
/// and area, closing with the Nova School Building & Design Fair; Term
/// 7 (Weeks 25-28) angles, shape properties, and coordinates; Term 8
/// (Weeks 29-32) tables, line graphs, and averages; and Term 9 (Weeks
/// 33-36) a full review, mock test, and graduation. See
